{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>והיה לבער.</b> To kindle. And behold, it is explained: there is one who warms with fire, and there is one who kindles it, like ואש נשקה (Psalms 78:21), like the form in בער." "<b>ויסגוד.</b> Known in Aramaic and in the language of Kedar."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra appears to use the root בער to illustrate a Hebrew/Aramaic cognate pair; the logic is compressed and left as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:58.507846856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}